  "id": "beja_music",
  "name": "Beja music (eastern Sudan lyre song and electric bands)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Beja peoples of eastern Sudan's Red Sea Hills and coast, around Port Sudan and Kassala, sung in Bedawiyet and Tigre. Its core is song accompanied by the basankob bowl lyre, for which the kissar card stands in; in Port Sudan, bands such as Noori & His Dorpa Band carry the lyre riffs onto an electrified lyre-guitar hybrid, for which the electric guitar card stands in, and add saxophone, bass and drums.",
  "recipe": "classic modern beja music, functional Song, African pop branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. kissar, clean strummed single coil electric guitar, saxophone, electric bass, machine hammered symmetric pattern organized rows full lathed both sides lathed drum kit. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
